menu "Companion secure storage"

config COMPANION_REQUIRE_ENCRYPTED_NVS
    bool "Require pre-provisioned HMAC-backed NVS encryption"
    default n
    help
        Production/manufacturing guard for persisted Wi-Fi and enrolled-device
        credentials. When enabled, the build must also enable NVS encryption
        with the HMAC key-protection scheme. At boot Companion verifies that
        the configured eFuse key block is already provisioned with HMAC_UP
        before nvs_flash_init() is allowed to run. Companion never burns the
        HMAC eFuse key automatically.

config COMPANION_NVS_HMAC_KEY_ID
    int "Companion HMAC eFuse key slot"
    range 0 5
    default 0
    help
        Key slot (KEY0..KEY5) that Companion expects manufacturing to have
        provisioned with purpose HMAC_UP. This value is compiled in all builds
        so the preflight code stays build-covered, but it is enforced only when
        COMPANION_REQUIRE_ENCRYPTED_NVS is enabled. In secure mode it must equal
        CONFIG_NVS_SEC_HMAC_EFUSE_KEY_ID.

endmenu
